  "note": "Indicators of compromise for npm supply-chain incidents. Data-only: add entries here, never in ioc-sweep.mjs. The September 2025 maintainer-account compromise was reconciled 2026-08-05 against two independent published analyses (Wiz and Semgrep), which agree on all 25 name@version pairs. The August 2026 keyv/cacheable compromise was reconciled 2026-08-06 against Socket and Aikido: they agree on nine name@version pairs, and disagree on file-entry-cache (Socket 11.1.7, Aikido 11.1.6) — both versions are listed rather than picking a winner, because a spurious extra version costs an investigation while a missing one costs a miss. ecto@5.0.1 and @thiennq/docs-viewer@1.6.2 are single-source and retained on the same basis as color@5.0.1. Socket additionally flags @keyv/redis, @keyv/sqlite and @keyv/mongo at 6.0.0 as suspect but confirms the payload only in keyv itself; they are deliberately NOT listed, because shipping an unconfirmed indicator is what the 2026-08-05 reconciliation removed. KNOWN LIMITATION: neither wave is enumerated in full — Shai-Hulud was reported at 500+ packages and the August 2026 campaign at 400-2200+ across 1381 versions; both are covered beyond these pairs only behaviourally (exfiltration endpoints, planted workflow, TruffleHog usage, phishing domain, Bun dropper URL, stage-2 payload path). Consult a live advisory feed before treating a clean sweep as exhaustive.",
